# Cupcake Hardware Self-Test
#
# RPi : copy as  /boot/firmware/cupcake-selftest.txt
#
# The file only needs to exist; its contents are ignored. It is read on every
# boot and deleted once the self-test has been queued, so each copy runs the
# self-test once.
#
# What it checks:
#   - first boot completed, secrets generated, services and API running
#   - with a USB stick labelled CUPCAKE-DATA attached: the stick is configured
#     as storage, a full backup is written onto it, and the Pi reboots once to
#     confirm the storage survives a restart
#   - board model, memory, temperature, power and throttling problems, SD card
#     write speed, boot time and failed services
#
# Results are written to the boot partition, readable on any computer:
#   cupcake-selftest-report.txt   summary
#   cupcake-selftest-report.json  full report
#
# The activity LED shows the outcome: a heartbeat for pass, a fast blink for
# failure.
#
# The self-test leaves test data on the device. Reflash before real use.
